PRACTICAL – 8
Title:

Analysis of Network Traffic for Android Device using HTTP Toolkit

Aim:

To analyze network traffic generated by an Android application using HTTP Toolkit.

Objectives:
To understand network traffic analysis in Android applications
To install and configure HTTP Toolkit
To capture and inspect HTTP/HTTPS requests from Android devices
To analyze API calls, headers, and responses
To identify insecure network communication and sensitive data exposure
Procedure:
(i) Install HTTP Toolkit

Open terminal and run:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install snapd -y

Install HTTP Toolkit:

sudo snap install httptoolkit
(ii) Launch HTTP Toolkit

Run:

httptoolkit
(iii) Start Android Emulator/Device
Launch Android emulator (AVD) or connect Android device
Ensure USB debugging is enabled

Verify connection:

adb devices
(iv) Configure HTTP Toolkit for Android
Open HTTP Toolkit

Select:

Android Device
Follow setup instructions provided by HTTP Toolkit
Configure proxy settings automatically
(v) Install Certificate
Install HTTP Toolkit certificate on emulator/device
Allow HTTPS traffic interception
(vi) Launch Android Application

Install APK if required:

adb install DivaApplication.apk

Open and use the application.

(vii) Capture Network Traffic

Observe:

HTTP requests
HTTPS requests
API endpoints
Request headers
Response bodies
Authentication tokens
(viii) Analyze Security Issues

Check for:

Unencrypted traffic
Sensitive information exposure
Weak authentication
Insecure APIs
Observation:
HTTP Toolkit successfully intercepted Android application traffic
HTTP/HTTPS requests and responses were captured
API endpoints, headers, and payloads were analyzed
Sensitive data and insecure communication patterns were identified
Result:

Network traffic analysis of the Android application was successfully performed using HTTP Toolkit. Requests, responses, and API communications were monitored to identify insecure network behavior and sensitive data exposure.

Viva Questions:
Q: What is HTTP Toolkit?

👉 Tool used to intercept and analyze HTTP/HTTPS traffic.

Q: Why install certificate in Android device?

👉 To decrypt and inspect HTTPS traffic securely.

Q: What can be analyzed using HTTP Toolkit?

👉 API requests, headers, responses, tokens, and network communication.

Q: Why is network traffic analysis important?

👉 To identify insecure communication and sensitive data leakage.

Important Commands
httptoolkit
adb devices
adb install DivaApplication.apk
